      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(qa): retire the standalone Matrix QA runtime",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMatrix release QA had two independently maintained execution systems: the QA Lab scenario host and a standalone `qa-matrix` plugin with its own runtime, catalog, profiles, artifacts, retries, and workflow jobs. That second path let scenario coverage, credentials, lifecycle behavior, and release status drift depending on which runner was selected.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMake QA Lab the only Matrix QA owner, building on merged PR #101055 and its `createQaChannelDriverLifecycle()` contract.\n\n- Removes the `extensions/qa-matrix` package/plugin, registrations, dependencies, private runtime/catalog, Matrix-only artifacts, and standalone release orchestration.\n- Keeps `pnpm openclaw qa matrix` only as a thin QA Lab selector for the shared scenario/profile host and `live:matrix` adapter.\n- Converts all 81 former adapter-executed Matrix definitions from `execution.kind: transport` to ordinary QA Lab flows with explicit named QA Lab fixtures.\n- Removes the adapter `runScenario` API, Matrix scenario-id dispatcher, adapter-owned retry policy, and adapter-owned timeout policy.\n- Keeps scenario selection, sequencing, retries, timeouts, assertions, artifacts, and failure reporting in QA Lab. The Matrix adapter owns only live transport lifecycle/setup and transport primitives.\n- Preserves the historical 94-ID migration ledger while attaching every legacy behavior to an existing QA Lab scenario. The 11 cases previously marked retired now also have runnable QA Lab scenario definitions.\n\nNo compatibility fallback is retained because it would recreate a second Matrix execution path.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMaintainers and release managers get one Matrix QA implementation and evidence format.\n\n- `qa matrix --profile release` remains the focused two-scenario release selector.\n- `qa matrix --profile fast` retains 11 scenarios.\n- `qa matrix --profile transport` retains 50 scenarios.\n- Media and E2EE profiles retain their previous membership.\n- `qa matrix` / `--profile all` retains the 92-scenario default profile, with two legacy explicit-only scenarios still excluded from the default exactly as before.\n- Per-scenario provider mode, Matrix config, retry count, timeout, artifacts, and failure semantics are preserved.\n\nThere is no shipped Matrix channel runtime change. Packaged OpenClaw releases continue to omit private QA Lab tooling.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Dependency/base proof:\n  - Rebased onto `origin/main` `3d206140f3f0ab639cebb67fa20c93c15296c61f`.\n  - PR #101055 is merged and its channel-driver lifecycle seam remains the only live Matrix lifecycle path.\n- Migration parity:\n  - All 81 former `kind: transport` definitions are now `kind: flow` and bind to unique named QA Lab fixtures.\n  - Mechanical comparison against the pre-refactor definitions found 0 mismatches across channel, provider mode, Matrix config, retry count, and timeout.\n  - Profile assertions: `all=92`, `fast=11`, `release=2`, `transport=50`, `media=7`, `e2ee-smoke=8`, `e2ee-deep=18`, `e2ee-cli=9`.\n  - The 94-entry legacy ledger has no missing or duplicate IDs, and every entry resolves to a QA Lab scenario.\n- Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox: `tbx_01kwyj4z2n1y4msce7qajwdavb` (`golden-hermit`):\n  - SDK + QA Lab focused proof: 125 tests passed.\n  - Matrix observer/topology follow-up: 29 tests passed.\n  - `check:test-types` passed.\n  - Targeted oxlint and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Review:\n  - Final branch autoreview found and prompted a real fix for rooms that exclude the driver account; the adapter now observes each room with a joined non-SUT account.\n  - Fresh final whole-branch Codex autoreview on `e7ad52ae49ec6eab851ff850d48aa263e27e404c`: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Exact-target release proof dispatched:\n  - Focused `qa-live-matrix`: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28879900596\n  - Full manual QA Live: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28879902435\n",
        "branch": "dallin/unify-matrix-release-qa",
